# Global standards

MarginMint is an e-commerce seller operations and profit intelligence SaaS. Every change must protect financial correctness, workspace isolation, and a premium B2B experience.

## Before editing

- Read surrounding code, types, and related tests before changing behavior.
- Reuse existing components, hooks, utilities, and domain modules; do not duplicate.
- Follow the established layering in `architecture.mdc` (UI → services → domain / adapters / repositories).
- Prefer extending existing patterns over introducing new frameworks or abstractions.

## Change discipline

- Keep diffs focused on the requested task; avoid drive-by refactors.
- Never silently remove or weaken existing functionality; call out intentional removals.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies and parallel implementations of the same concern.
- Document significant architectural decisions (ADR note, PR description, or `AGENTS.md` update).

## Completeness and honesty

- Never leave fake buttons, dead links, or incomplete interactions without an explicit explanation in the UI or PR.
- Never hardcode production business metrics (live GMV, margins, fee rates, or KPIs) as static demo values in product paths.
- Never claim an integration, test, import, migration, or operation succeeded without verifying it ran successfully.
- After substantive changes, run the relevant typecheck, lint, unit, and/or e2e commands that exist in the repo and report results honestly.

## Keep the project honest and current

- Demo, imported and synced data must always be labelled; never mix demo and real records in one list.
- When behaviour, commands, env vars or architecture change, update `AGENTS.md`, the relevant `docs/` page and these rules in the same change (see `documentation.mdc`).
- Remove dead code and unused dependencies instead of leaving them "for later".

## Code quality

- Write maintainable, readable, type-safe code aligned with `typescript.mdc`.
- Financial math follows `financial-logic.mdc`; security follows `database-security.mdc`.
- Detailed rules live in `.cursor/rules/`; keep this file as the always-on checklist.
